@@section 1
@@title SQ-MB monster box vaults, 2026-10-30 ([mob_block_tweaks.md](../mob_block_tweaks.md) 2.9, TODO `mobs/tweaks #5`, MT-34 to MT-37, MT-47 to MT-50)
@@date 2026-10-30
@@jars creativecompat creativeworldgen
@@sources feature_writeup/mob_block_tweaks.md
@@text
@@text Needs patcherMod 1.1.04 from 2026-10-30 22:59 or later (`mobs/MonsterBoxVault`, `MonsterBoxBlockEntityMixin`,
@@text `CreateBreakerMonsterBoxMixin`), the KubeJS block properties, block tags and reward table, and
@@text `quark-common.toml` with `Enable Extra Loot Table = false`. Group A (superflat), Normal difficulty, a bot player.
@@text For SQ-MB-04 set `[monster_box] cooldownTicks = 200` in the scratch `creativeengineering-common.toml` before boot.
@@text
@@text | ID | Group | Commands | Expected | If it fails |
@@text |---|---|---|---|---|
## SQ-MB-01 | monster box mixins and reward table
@group A
@commands Boot; grep latest.log for `MonsterBoxBlockEntityMixin`, `CreateBreakerMonsterBoxMixin`, `monster box reward`
@pass no mixin apply error, no missing-table warning
@fails mixin target or SRG name wrong; table path
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb passed
bootreject (Mixin apply failed|InvalidInjectionException).*(MonsterBoxBlockEntityMixin|CreateBreakerMonsterBoxMixin)
bootreject (?i)monster.?box.*(missing|not found)

## SQ-MB-02 | monster box stays and records its wave (Normal difficulty, bot next to it)
@group A
@commands `/setblock ~2 ~ ~ quark:monster_box`; tp the bot next to it; wait 3 s; `/execute if block ~2 ~ ~ quark:monster_box`; `/data get block ~2 ~ ~`
@pass box still there; NBT has `creativeengineering:phase` 1b and a `creativeengineering:wave` list of 5-8 UUIDs
@fails redirect not applied (box gone) or claim scan missed the mobs
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
> difficulty normal
> setblock 20 -60 -20 quark:monster_box
> tp qa 18 -60 -20
sleep 4
> execute if block 20 -60 -20 quark:monster_box
> data get block 20 -60 -20
expect Test passed
expect creativeengineering:phase": 1b
expect creativeengineering:wave
look the wave list holds 5 to 8 UUIDs

## SQ-MB-03 | wave dead -> one reward stack, rest phase
@group A
@commands `/kill @e[type=!player,type=!item,distance=..20]`; wait 2 s; `/data get block ~2 ~ ~`; count `@e[type=item,distance=..3]`
@pass phase 2b, `until` = game time + 72000; exactly 1 item entity at the box
@fails wave check or reward roll
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
# scratch-only: no mob drops, so the item count is the reward alone; bot leaves at once so the 200-tick cooldown
# does not re-arm the box with the bot beside it (SQ-MB-04 needs phase 0 first) and the bot cannot pick up the reward
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item]
> gamerule doMobLoot false
> tp qa 0 -60 0
> execute positioned 20 -60 -20 run kill @e[type=!minecraft:player,type=!minecraft:item,distance=..24]
sleep 3
> data get block 20 -60 -20
> execute positioned 20 -60 -20 if entity @e[type=item,distance=..3]
expect creativeengineering:phase": 2b
expect creativeengineering:until
expect Test passed, count: 1
> gamerule doMobLoot true
look until = game time + 72000 normally; this boot has cooldownTicks 200, so until = game time + 200

## SQ-MB-04 | cooldown ends, a new wave starts (cooldownTicks 200)
@group A
@commands (cooldownTicks 200) after SQ-MB-03 wait 11 s with the bot away, then bring it back
@pass phase 0b, then a new wave and phase 1b
@fails cooldown never ends
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb passed
> tp qa 0 -60 0
> kill @e[type=item]
sleep 12
> data get block 20 -60 -20
> tp qa 18 -60 -20
sleep 4
> data get block 20 -60 -20
expect creativeengineering:phase": 0b
expect creativeengineering:phase": 1b
> execute positioned 20 -60 -20 run kill @e[type=!minecraft:player,distance=..24]

## SQ-MB-05 | monster box mining tags
@group A
@commands `/data get block ~2 ~ ~` on a box in phase 2; check the block's destroy speed with `/kubejs` dump or WTHIT (client)
@pass hardness 50, needs diamond pickaxe
@fails startup modification or tags not loaded
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
> execute if block 20 -60 -20 #minecraft:mineable/pickaxe
> execute if block 20 -60 -20 #minecraft:needs_diamond_tool
count Test passed == 2
look hardness 25 per the changelog (queue row says 50): check with WTHIT in the client block (CQ-MB-08)

## SQ-MB-06 | Create drill cannot break it
@group A
@commands Powered Create drill facing a box, 30 s
@pass box still there
@fails Create mixin not applied
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
> setblock 22 -60 -20 create:creative_motor[facing=west]
> setblock 21 -60 -20 create:mechanical_drill[facing=west]
sleep 30
> execute if block 20 -60 -20 quark:monster_box
expect Test passed
look if the drill did not turn (motor facing wrong), set facing=east on the motor and rerun the row
> fill 21 -60 -20 22 -60 -20 minecraft:air

## SQ-MB-07 | vaultMode off: box breaks after spawning (Quark behaviour)
@group A
@commands `[monster_box] vaultMode = false`, boot, repeat SQ-MB-02
@pass box breaks after spawning (Quark behaviour)
@fails off switch
